@zadjii-msft 
Actually the only function from std that would make this code shorter is `regex_replace`, but I measured it to be about 10 times slower than this approach.

@DHowett-MSFT 
The cumulative (non char-by-char) approach is about 10% faster (for strings, see below) but somewhat more complicated. Choose your tradeoff :)

So actually, it looks like `std::ostringstream` doesn't perform preallocation, so frequent  writes are slower than with `std::string` and `append()`, up to 10 times for char-by-char append. Would you know? 
So I quess we could leave it as is for now and eventually replace `std::ostringstream` (everywhere) with some wrapper that does preallocation, when we get into optimization stage.

